This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   The user's sole explicit instruction (the initial, and only, user message) was: "Build the cinema seat-booking web application described in spec/README.md, as the React application already set up in this Nx workspace (Nx project `cinescope` in apps/cinescope); its stack is described in spec/stack.md. The work is split into tickets in spec/tickets/; implement them in order. spec/README.md is the complete specification: do not ask any questions, and where it is silent choose the simplest option that satisfies it. Finish only when every ticket is done and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds."

   Key constraints from spec/README.md that must be honored throughout:
   - Package manager is pnpm only (never npm/yarn).
   - App must stay on port 4200.
   - Do NOT add dependencies — everything needed is already installed.
   - Do NOT edit db.json by hand.
   - Desktop-only viewport (1280×720+), all text in English.
   - Must use the UI library (MUI) for every button (including day/screening buttons), text field, checkbox, toast, and the datepicker; the seat map/legend/selected-seats panel are hand-drawn by the app itself.
   - Exact `data-testid` contract (section 9) must be honored verbatim — no renaming/abbreviating/prefixing, and these testids must not appear on any other elements.
   - Full acceptance criteria list (AC-01 to AC-69, section 10) must all be met; ticket 07 requires walking the whole app against the spec and ensuring `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds.
   - Things explicitly out of scope (section 11): user accounts, real payment processing, seat locking between concurrent customers, updating occupiedSeats after reservation, posters/images, mobile/responsive layouts, keyboard navigation/ARIA beyond browser/library defaults, translations.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Nx 23 monorepo, Vite-based React 19 app, React Router 6 (`BrowserRouter`), MUI 9 (`@mui/material`, `@mui/icons-material`), MUI X Date Pickers 9 with dayjs adapter, SCSS (CSS Modules), Vitest 4 + Testing Library (dom, react) for unit tests, ESLint flat config.
   - json-server 0.17.4 backend serving db.json at http://localhost:3000 (GET /movies, /movies/:id, /screenings, /screenings?date=, /screenings?movieId=, /screenings/:id, POST /reservations).
   - sessionStorage-backed "booking in progress" state machine with strict route-guard rules (section 3.1) — different rules for seat-map route (screening must exist) vs summary/checkout routes (booking must be unpaid, match screeningId, have ≥1 seat) vs confirmation route (booking must be paid).
   - CSS Grid-based auditorium layout using a fixed 28-track template per row so all rows align identically; explicit `gridColumn` inline styles computed via a `seatColumnTrack` mapping function to handle the entrance gap (rows 1-10 omit columns 1-4) and two aisles (between col 4/5 and col 20/21).
   - Seat/couch domain model: seat identifiers `R<row>C<col>`; couches occupy two adjacent columns and are toggled/priced as a single unit; selection count where a couch always contributes 2 identifiers to `booking.seats`, making `seats.length` double as the "n seats selected" count without extra bookkeeping.
   - Toast system: single toast at a time, auto-dismiss after 4000ms, via MUI Snackbar.
   - Form validation logic for checkout matching exact spec wording for required/invalid messages, with "touched" (blurred) state gating message visibility, and a submit-time "mark all touched" behavior.
   - MUI v9 API specifics learned during implementation: `StackProps` no longer accepts `alignItems`/other system props directly (must go through `sx`); `TextField` no longer supports `InputLabelProps`/`FormHelperTextProps` (removed) — must use `slotProps={{ inputLabel: {...}, formHelperText: {...} }}` instead.
   - Node 26 provides global `fetch`; environment resolves "localhost" inconsistently between IPv4/IPv6 in ad hoc `node -e` calls, but services actually bind and work correctly (confirmed via `http://[::1]:PORT`).
   - No browser-automation tooling (chromium-cli, lsof, playwright, puppeteer) available in this sandbox; the `/run` skill's standard browser-driven verification pattern could not be executed, and installing such tooling would violate the spec's "do not add dependencies" rule.

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **spec/README.md, spec/stack.md, spec/tickets/*.md** — read in full; these define the complete contract (data model, endpoints, routes, booking lifecycle, all screen specs, data-testid contract, and AC-01–AC-69). No edits made; used purely as the source of truth.

   - **apps/cinescope/src/api/types.ts** (created) — `Movie`, `Screening`, `ReservationCustomer`, `Reservation`, `NewReservation = Omit<Reservation, 'id'>`.

   - **apps/cinescope/src/api/client.ts** (created) — `BASE_URL = 'http://localhost:3000'`; generic `request<T>(path, init)` throwing on network error or non-2xx; exports `getMovies`, `getMovie(id)`, `getScreenings({date?, movieId?})`, `getScreening(id)`, `createReservation(reservation)`.

   - **apps/cinescope/src/lib/seats.ts** (created, later edited) — central seat/pricing/geometry module. Final important exports:
     ```ts
     export const ROW_COUNT = 15;
     export const COLUMN_COUNT = 24;
     export const COUCH_ROW = 15;
     export const MAX_SEATS_PER_BOOKING = 10;
     export type SeatState = 'available' | 'selected' | 'unavailable' | 'accessible';
     export const SEAT_COLORS: Record<SeatState, string> = {
       available: '#2E7D32', selected: '#F9A825', unavailable: '#C62828', accessible: '#1565C0',
     };
     export function seatId(row, column) => `R${row}C${column}`;
     export function isCouchRow(row) => row === COUCH_ROW;
     export function isAccessible(row, column) => row === 1 && column >= 10 && column <= 15;
     export function priceForRow(row) // 1-5:25, 6-10:32, 11-14:39, else 89
     export function formatPrice(amount) => `${amount.toFixed(2)} PLN`;
     export function seatColumnTrack(column) // col<=4: col+1; col<=20: col+2; else col+3
     export const LEFT_LABEL_TRACK = 1, AISLE_TRACK_1 = 6, AISLE_TRACK_2 = 23, RIGHT_LABEL_TRACK = 28, GRID_TRACK_COUNT = 28;
     export function couchPairs() // [[1,2],[3,4],...,[23,24]]
     export type RowCell = {kind:'seat',column} | {kind:'couch',columnStart,columnEnd};
     export function buildRowCells(row) // couch pairs for row15; else seats from column 5 (rows<=10) or 1 (rows 11-14) through 24
     export function seatState(row, column, occupied, selected): SeatState
     export interface SummaryItem { row, columnStart, columnEnd: number|null, identifiers: string[], price }
     export function toSummaryItems(seats: string[]): SummaryItem[] // grouped & sorted by row then column
     export function seatLabel(item) => columnEnd!==null ? `Couch ${a}-${b}` : `${col}`  // used by Summary screen
     function panelSeatLabel(item) => columnEnd!==null ? `${a}-${b}` : `${col}`  // used only by selectedSeatsByRow (NO "Couch" prefix — fixed bug, see below)
     export function selectedSeatsByRow(seats): {row, label}[] // uses panelSeatLabel now
     ```
     **Important fix**: originally `selectedSeatsByRow` called `seatLabel` (the Summary-style "Couch a-b" label), which is wrong for the section 5.5 selected-seats panel (spec example shows `Row 15: 1-2`, not `Row 15: Couch 1-2`). Caught via a failing unit test; fixed by introducing the private `panelSeatLabel` and switching `selectedSeatsByRow` to use it.

